This component already has a condition for `shouldUseNarrowLayout`. It seems that the mobile version of the skeleton is already implemented here. This simplifies things.

The problem is that `src/components/Search/index.tsx` is not using `SearchRowSkeleton` correctly. It is being used without considering the mobile layout.

Let's re-examine `src/components/Search/index.tsx`, specifically the `shouldShowLoadingState` block.

```typescript
if (shouldShowLoadingState) {
    return (
        <>
            <SearchPageHeader
                queryJSON={queryJSON}
                hash={hash}
            />

            {/* We only want to display the skeleton for the status filters the first time we load them for a specific data type */}
            {searchResults?.search?.type === type ? (
                <SearchStatusBar
                    type={type}
                    status={status}
                    resetOffset={resetOffset}
                />
            ) : (
                <SearchStatusSkeleton shouldAnimate />
            )}
            <SearchRowSkeleton shouldAnimate />
        </>
    );
}
```

The issue is that `SearchRowSkeleton` is rendered without any props that would indicate that it should render the mobile version. The component itself handles the logic, so this should be fine.

Let me go back to the issue description, maybe I misunderstood something. > [Search v1] Implement mobile specific loading skeleton

This means that the current skeleton is not mobile-specific, and I need to create one. The code in `SearchRowSkeleton` for `shouldUseNarrowLayout` is probably the desktop version, and I need to create a new one for mobile.

So my initial plan was correct.

1.  Create a new component `src/components/Skeletons/MobileSearchSkeleton.tsx`.
2.  I will modify `src/components/Search/index.tsx` to use this new component when `isSmallScreenWidth` is true.

I will start by creating the new file. I'll copy the content of `SearchRowSkeleton.tsx` and adapt it for mobile. I will remove the desktop-specific code and simplify the layout.

